    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keepusing(pgmode pgna
> tion pgpartz pgpartnr pglabgro pgsndjob pgfamstd)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keepusing(plh0004 plb01
> 76_h plb0585 plb0584 plb0517 plc0177 plc0178 plh0308_v2 pld0133 plc0177 plc01
> 78)
(label cid already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

.         drop eintritt erstbefr austritt psample letztbef sampreg netto nett1 
> casemat pop todjahr todinfo immiyear germborn corigin gebmonat loc1989 migbac
> k miginfo germborninfo corigininfo immiyearinfo sexor sexorinfo locinfo birth
> region birthregion_ew arefback arefinf rv_id prgroup pbleib phrf phrf0 phrf1 
> piyear

.         label language EN // change language of the labels to English

.         save "$DATA/h3_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/5%-sample/h3_dataset.dta saved

.         
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS *
.  
. *We include only families with 1-2 children. If participants had children dur
> ing our included panel years, this was reflected in sumkids but not biokids, 
> so we use sumkids as our basis for exclusion.
. drop if sumkids>2 | sumkids==0
(17,141 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include data limited to the years 2000 to 2020.
. drop if syear<2000 | syear>2020
(0 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include only responses from individuals over the age of 18.
. drop if bioage <18
(3,956 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include only Computer-Assisted Personal Interviews (CAPI) to avoid experi
> menter effects
. drop if pgmode!=140
(7,651 observations deleted)

.         
.         
. * GENERATE VARIABLES *
. *Tidy Control Variables
. rename bioage Age

. rename sex Male

. gen Income = pglabgro if pglabgro>=0
(2,712 missing values generated)

. replace Income = Income + pgsndjob if pgsndjob>0
(127 real changes made)

. replace pgnation = . if pgnation==-1
(1 real change made, 1 to missing)

. rename pgnation Nationality

. gen Partner_In_House = 1 if pld0133==1
(5,747 missing values generated)

. replace Partner_In_House = 0 if pld0133==2
(302 real changes made)

. replace Partner_In_House = 0 if pld0133==-2  
(5,071 real changes made)

. 
. 
. *Dependant variable
. *Our dependent variable will be a measure of the absolute difference in contr
> acted working hours between the Male (father) respondent and the Female (moth
> er) respondents within a household
. rename plb0176_h Work_Hours

. replace Work_Hours = 0 if Work_Hours==-2
(3,255 real changes made)

. drop if Work_Hours < 0
(109 observations deleted)

. drop if parid<0
(1,310 observations deleted)

. preserve

. bysort hid pid (syear): keep if _n == 1
(3,932 observations deleted)

. bysort hid: gen num_individuals = _N

. drop if num_individuals != 2
(343 observations deleted)

. gen is_male = (Male == 1)

. gen is_female = (Male == 2)

. collapse (sum) is_male is_female, by(hid)

. gen male_female_pair = .
(393 missing values generated)

. replace male_female_pair = 1 if is_male == 1 & is_female == 1
(389 real changes made)

. tempfile pairinfo

. save `pairinfo'
file C:\Users\DALBRE~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ST_3930_000003.tmp saved as .dta
    format

. restore

. merge m:1 hid using `pairinfo'

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                         1,232
        from master                     1,232  (_merge==1)
        from using                          0  (_merge==2)

    Matched                             3,829  (_merge==3)
    -----------------------------------------

. drop _merge

. 
. drop if male_female_pair != 1
(1,256 observations deleted)

. egen gender_count = total(male_female_pair), by(hid syear)

. drop if gender_count !=2
(179 observations deleted)

. preserve

. keep Work_Hours hid syear Male 

. reshape wide Work_Hours, i(hid syear) j(Male)
(j = 1 2)

Data                               Long   ->   Wide
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Number of observations            3,626   ->   1,813       
Number of variables                   4   ->   4           
j variable (2 values)              Male   ->   (dropped)
xij variables:
                             Work_Hours   ->   Work_Hours1 Work_Hours2
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

. gen diff_hours = Work_Hours1 - Work_Hours2

. gen abs_diff_hours = abs(diff_hours)

. tempfile diffs

. save `diffs'
file C:\Users\DALBRE~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ST_3930_000005.tmp saved as .dta
    format

. restore

. merge m:1 hid syear using `diffs'
(label syear_EN already defined)
(label plb0176_h_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                             3,626  (_merge==3)
    -----------------------------------------

. 
. 
. *Independant variables
. *We create a binary variable which takes the value 1 if a respondent answers 
> to one or more of the kidsex variables that the sex of their child is 'Female
> ' and '0' otherwise.
. gen At_least_One_Daughter = 0

. foreach var of varlist kidsex01-kidsex02 {
  2.     replace At_least_One_Daughter = 1 if `var' == 2
  3. }
(1,569 real changes made)
(834 real changes made)

. 
. *We also consider a pre (0) and post (1) treatment dummy coded as 0 before re
> spondents have a daughter and 1 after respondents have a daughter
. //gen After_Having_Daughter = 0
. //replace After_Having_Daughter = 1 if kidsex01==2 & (kidgeb01<=syear|syear<2
> 000)
. //replace After_Having_Daughter = 1 if kidsex02==2 & kidgeb02<=syear
. 
. *To use the Callaway & Sant'Anna (2021) method of staggered DiD as a robustne
> ss check we also generate a variable for the first year respondents had a dau
> ghter
. //gen First_Year_Daughter = .
. //replace First_Year_Daughter = kidgeb01 if kidsex01==2 & kidgeb01>2000
. //replace First_Year_Daughter = kidgeb02 if kidsex02==2 & kidsex01!=2 & kidge
> b02>2000
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 *
. *To test our third hypothesis that having daughters leads to more gender equa
> lity in the household, we conduct a staggered difference-in-difference estima
> tion with time (syear) and household-level (hid) fixed effects and clustered 
> standard errors. As our dependent variable, we match up all male-female partn
> ers in our sample using household codes, then calculate the absolute differen
> ce in contracted working hours between the Male (father) respondent and the F
> emale (mother) respondent (abs_diff_hours). As our independent variables, we 
> take the dummy for having a daughter or not (At_least_One_Daughter), a dummy 
> for pre and post having the first daughter (After_Having_Daughter) and an int
> eraction term of the two dummies (At_least_One_Daughter x After_Having_Daught
> er).
. 
. //preserve
. //bysort hid syear (Male): keep if _n == 1
. //reghdfe abs_diff_hours i.At_least_One_Daughter##i.After_Having_Daughter, ab
> sorb(hid syear) vce(cluster hid)
. //reghdfe abs_diff_hours i.At_least_One_Daughter##i.After_Having_Daughter Age
>  Income i.Nationality Partner_In_House, absorb(hid syear) vce(cluster hid)
. 
. // For robustness we also conduct a staggered diff in diff using the Callaway
>  & Sant'Anna (2021) method to account for treatment effect heterogeneity
. //csdid abs_diff_hours At_least_One_Daughter, ivar(hid) time(syear) gvar(Firs
> t_Year_Daughter) method(dripw) vce(cluster hid)
. //restore
. 
. //Cross-sectional analysis conducted rather than panel to make results compar
> able with data used for H1 and H4
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 - CROSS-SECTIONAL*
. // 2018 selected as year for cross-sectional analysis to make it directly com
> parable with the other hypotheses
. bysort hid syear (Male): keep if _n == 1
(1,813 observations deleted)

. reg abs_diff_hours At_least_One_Daughter if syear==2018

